  "narrative": "The accepted dataset-specific map is now centered on three families: feature_037 positivity is broadly associated with lower outcome_001; feature_003 positivity is associated with lower outcome_001 primarily in high-feature_036 contexts; and feature_010 positivity raises outcome_001 overall but is attenuated in high feature_038 and high feature_018 relative to their complements. The new proposals sharpen whether these patterns are conditional or merely compositional. For feature_003, two simple contrasts test high feature_018 or high feature_038 while explicitly excluding high feature_036; if those contrasts are near null, the earlier high-feature_018 and high-feature_038 feature_003 signals are likely driven by co-occurrence with high feature_036, whereas above-threshold effects would indicate modifier-independent lowering. Two feature_003 interactions then test, within high feature_036 itself, whether feature_018 or feature_038 further changes the size of the lowering association. For feature_010, the central unresolved question is overlap between the two accepted attenuation interactions. A joint high-feature_038/high-feature_018 simple contrast tests whether the combined modifier region retains a positive feature_010 contrast, while two interaction contrasts test whether feature_038 and feature_018 attenuation remains inside high feature_036, a context where the overall feature_010 association is strong. Another simple contrast tests high feature_018 while excluding high feature_036, directly asking whether the rejected positive high-feature_018 effect is explained by overlap with high feature_036. For feature_037, intersection contrasts test whether the broad lowering association remains strong in high-feature_018/non-high-feature_036 and low-feature_018/high-feature_036 regions, and one interaction tests whether the modest high-feature_018 modification seen overall persists outside high feature_038. Finally, one broad marginal comparison is added for feature_001 because many measured predictors remain unassessed. All anticipated directions refer to raw contrasts before signing, and all conclusions remain unadjusted associations within this supplied dataset rather than causal or generalizable claims.",
  "research_notes": "Current dataset-specific map: feature_037 lowering is broadly accepted across marginal, feature_018 extremes, mid bands, and much of feature_036/feature_038 non-high space; feature_003 lowering is accepted/validated in high feature_036 and several high-feature_036 joint/restricted contexts, while non-high feature_036 complements are rejected; feature_010 raising is accepted overall and across many non-high or mid modifier strata, with accepted attenuation interactions for high feature_038 and high feature_018. New registered comparisons now focus on specificity and overlap: feature_003 in high feature_018 or high feature_038 excluding high feature_036; feature_003-by-feature_018 and by-feature_038 interactions within high feature_036; feature_010 in joint high modifier space; feature_010-by-feature_038 and by-feature_018 interactions within high feature_036; feature_010 in high feature_018 excluding high feature_036; feature_037 intersection strata and a feature_037-by-feature_018 interaction outside high feature_038; plus one broad feature_001 marginal screen. Existing active broad and central claims still to analyze include H20, H21/H22, H24, H35-H36, H54-H58, H70/H89/H63/H64/H109-H110, and earlier refinements H116-H121. Avoid redundant analysis of accepted exact claims and do not request validation for already validated exact claims. All interpretations remain noncausal dataset associations."
